# Native compaction noninterference

## Confirmed source behavior

Runtime binding no longer starts pressure from a normal request's JSON/4 estimate.
Resumed transcript usage is diagnostic only because it is not attributed to this launch's current provider/model.
Native checkpoint observation, persisted checkpoint plus raw shrink validation, and numeric upstream overflow recovery remain.
Legacy local reactive preflight no longer synthesizes prompt-too-long HTTP errors.

Native compatible Responses checkpoint requests are sent upstream once before semantic map/reduce.
Only explicit HTTP no-output context rejection authorizes one bounded semantic recovery.
Unknown token count, UTF-8 byte size, ordinary HTTP 400/413, transport failures and partial streams are not recovery proof.
Byte-limited provider policy remains separate from token sizing.
Source fragments remain complete, Unicode-safe, and subject to an independent 64 MiB source cap.

## Executed verification

The exact-file runner `scripts/focused.py` removed inherited Runtime/Claude/provider environment,
selected a temporary Runtime config root and free loopback port before imports, and discovered only eight named files.
Result: 130 tests passed in 96.315 seconds. Full command output: `evidence/focused-tests.txt`.
Checks include native-first no auxiliary summary, unknown counts, large Unicode/tool payloads,
confirmed overflow plus real Responses map/reduce with raw orphan content retained,
one recovery maximum, error body fidelity, upstream model resolution, cancellation before billable summary,
identity/epoch isolation, stale resume usage noninterference, checkpoint/shrink safety and remote bypass.
Scoped changed-module py_compile and git diff --check passed.

## Limitations

This is fixture/runtime-code verification, not a live native CLI/provider acceptance run.
No native success or screen evidence is claimed. No live state, deployment, commit or push was touched.
Translated Chat/Anthropic semantic preflight retains its existing estimator-triggered policy; only native compatible Responses is native-first.
Cross-request single-flight was not added; individual fallback is bounded to one per request and map/reduce retains call/deadline limits.
In-flight synchronous summary HTTP calls cannot be interrupted; cancellation is checked before/between calls and before the final upstream retry.
The transport now accepts a model resolver; facade owner must bind the existing resolve_requested_model function.

## Integration follow-up

Translated Chat and Anthropic native checkpoint requests now also pass through
without estimator-driven summary unless confirmed-rejection marker is supplied.
Five dedicated passthrough regressions plus six provider semantic tests and
context suite passed (41 tests), see translated-compact-passthrough.txt in
10/20 integration-acceptance. No translated automatic replay was added.
Facade supplies resolve_requested_model to summary transport.
